# Mesen debugging (SA-1 vs SNES)

Mesen exposes both a regular **Debugger** (SNES CPU) and an **SA-1 Debugger**.

## Which to use

| Work | Prefer |
|---|---|
| PIXI sprites, GPS/blocks, sprite/block interaction | **SA-1 Debugger** |
| UberASM (level/gamemode/overworld ASM) | **SNES Debugger** (regular) |

If breakpoints or PC/stepping look wrong, switch debugger CPU context before assuming the code is broken.

## Automated MCP / test harness

- Emulation control and RAM reads go through patched Mesen MCP (`tools/test/mesen/`).
- `run_frames` must wait on SA-1 game frame `$3013` (DP), not only PPU frame count — PPU can advance while the SNES CPU sits in the `LDA $10` / `BEQ` wait loop.
- For PIXI-focused checks, read/step with SA-1 CPU type in mind when using MCP CPU tools; for UberASM, SNES (`cpu_type` 0).
